.TH WS2SOCKET 1 "January 2026" "ws2socket 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ws2socket \- WebSocket to TCP socket proxy daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ws2socket
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ws2socket
is a WebSocket to TCP socket proxy that allows WebSocket clients to connect to arbitrary TCP servers. It accepts WebSocket connections and forwards traffic bidirectionally between the WebSocket client and a target TCP server.

This is a pure C implementation of the websockify proxy, designed for embedded systems and Yocto-based Linux distributions without Python dependencies. It provides low memory footprint, fast startup, and minimal resource usage.

The proxy performs WebSocket protocol handshake according to RFC 6455, handles frame encoding/decoding, and transparently bridges WebSocket and raw TCP communications.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-listen " " \fIADDRESS\fR:\fIPORT\fR
Listen address and port for incoming WebSocket connections. Default is 0.0.0.0:6080.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Listen port (alternative to specifying in \-\-listen). Default is 6080.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target " " \fIHOST\fR:\fIPORT\fR
Target TCP server address and port to proxy connections to. This option is required unless using a token-based target mapping.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cert " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to SSL/TLS certificate file in PEM format for secure WebSocket (wss://) connections.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to SSL/TLS private key file in PEM format. Required when using \-\-cert.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose logging output. Sets log level to DEBUG for detailed diagnostic information.
.TP
.BR \-\-log-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Write log messages to the specified file instead of console output.
.TP
.BR \-\-daemon
Run as a background daemon process. Detaches from the controlling terminal and runs in the background.
.TP
.BR \-\-pid-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Write the daemon process ID to the specified file. Useful for process management and service control.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Basic proxy to a VNC server:
.B ws2socket \-\-listen 0.0.0.0:6080 \-\-target 127.0.0.1:5900
.TP
Proxy with verbose logging:
.B ws2socket \-v \-\-log-file /var/log/ws2socket.log \-\-listen 0.0.0.0:6080 \-\-target 192.168.1.100:22
.TP
Secure WebSocket proxy (WSS):
.B ws2socket \-\-cert /etc/ssl/certs/server.pem \-\-key /etc/ssl/private/server.key \-\-listen 0.0.0.0:443 \-\-target example.com:22
.TP
Run as daemon with PID file:
.B ws2socket \-\-daemon \-\-pid-file /var/run/ws2socket.pid \-\-log-file /var/log/ws2socket.log \-\-listen 0.0.0.0:6080 \-\-target 127.0.0.1:5900
.TP
Proxy SSH connections over WebSocket:
.B ws2socket \-\-listen 0.0.0.0:8080 \-\-target 127.0.0.1:22
.SH PROTOCOL
.B ws2socket
implements the WebSocket protocol as specified in RFC 6455. It handles:
.IP \(bu 2
WebSocket handshake (HTTP Upgrade)
.IP \(bu 2
Frame encoding and decoding
.IP \(bu 2
Data frame masking/unmasking
.IP \(bu 2
Control frames (ping, pong, close)
.IP \(bu 2
Fragmented messages
.IP \(bu 2
Binary and text data types

The proxy transparently converts between WebSocket frames and raw TCP streams, allowing web applications to communicate with TCP services.
.SH USE CASES
.TP
.B VNC Access
Provide browser-based VNC access using noVNC or similar WebSocket VNC clients.
.TP
.B SSH over WebSocket
Enable SSH access through firewalls that only allow HTTP/HTTPS traffic.
.TP
.B Terminal Access
Provide web-based terminal access to embedded devices.
.TP
.B Serial Port Access
Bridge WebSocket connections to serial devices for IoT applications.
.TP
.B Legacy Protocol Modernization
Expose legacy TCP services through modern WebSocket APIs.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM, SIGINT
Gracefully shutdown the proxy. Closes all active connections, flushes logs, removes PID file, and exits cleanly.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/run/ws2socket.pid
Default PID file location when running as daemon (can be changed with \-\-pid-file).
.TP
.I /var/log/ws2socket.log
Default log file location when using \-\-log-file option.
.TP
.I /etc/ssl/certs/
Typical location for SSL/TLS certificates.
.TP
.I /etc/ssl/private/
Typical location for SSL/TLS private keys.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B ws2socket
returns the following exit codes:
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
General error (configuration, initialization, runtime error)
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments or configuration
.SH LOGGING
The proxy supports multiple log levels:
.TP
.B DEBUG (0)
Detailed diagnostic information for troubleshooting
.TP
.B INFO (1)
Informational messages about normal operation
.TP
.B WARN (2)
Warning messages for potential issues
.TP
.B ERROR (3)
Error messages for recoverable failures
.TP
.B CRITICAL (4)
Critical errors requiring immediate attention

Logs can be directed to:
.IP \(bu 2
Console (stderr) - default
.IP \(bu 2
File - using \-\-log-file option
.IP \(bu 2
Syslog - configurable in code
.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.TP
.B SSL/TLS
Always use SSL/TLS certificates (\-\-cert, \-\-key) in production environments to encrypt WebSocket traffic.
.TP
.B Authentication
The current version does not include built-in authentication. Use external authentication mechanisms (reverse proxy, firewall rules) or implement token-based authentication.
.TP
.B Network Exposure
Limit listen addresses to specific interfaces when possible. Avoid binding to 0.0.0.0 on publicly accessible systems.
.TP
.B Firewall
Configure firewall rules to restrict access to authorized clients only.
.SH PERFORMANCE
.B ws2socket
is designed for embedded systems with:
.IP \(bu 2
Small binary size: ~55 KB (dynamic), ~30 KB (stripped)
.IP \(bu 2
Low memory footprint: <5 MB typical usage
.IP \(bu 2
Fast startup: <100ms initialization time
.IP \(bu 2
Thread-safe operations with minimal locking
.IP \(bu 2
Configurable buffer sizes for memory optimization
.SH LIMITATIONS
Current implementation has the following known limitations:
.IP \(bu 2
WebSocket frame codec requires completion for full functionality
.IP \(bu 2
HTTP request parsing is partially implemented
.IP \(bu 2
Token-based target mapping not yet implemented
.IP \(bu 2
No built-in authentication mechanism
.IP \(bu 2
Single-threaded event loop (select-based)
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B ws2socket
requires:
.IP \(bu 2
OpenSSL >= 3.0 (libssl, libcrypto) for cryptography and SSL/TLS
.IP \(bu 2
POSIX threads (pthread) for synchronization
.IP \(bu 2
Standard C library (libc)
.SH YOCTO INTEGRATION
.B ws2socket
is designed for Yocto Project integration:
.IP \(bu 2
CMake build system (native to Yocto)
.IP \(bu 2
No Python dependencies
.IP \(bu 2
LGPL v3 license (Yocto-compatible)
.IP \(bu 2
Minimal footprint suitable for embedded targets
.IP \(bu 2
Compatible with Yocto Scarthgap 5 and later

See IMPLEMENTATION.md for BitBake recipe template.
